untry>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TASHIRO YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI, SHU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NUKUI, KATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TASHIRO, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An exciting radiation source (4) is arranged on or near one focal axis X-X of an elliptic cylinder or cone composed chiefly of quartz, and an amplification medium (3) is arranged on or near the other focal axis Y-Y. The exciting light falls on the amplification medium efficiently because of the geometrical property that light from one focus of an ellipse converges on the other focus.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, on a agencé une source de rayonnement excitateur (4) sur ou à proximité d'un axe focal X-X d'un cylindre elliptique ou cône composé principalement de quartz, et on a agencé un milieu d'amplification (3) sur ou à proximité de l'autre axe focal Y-Y. La lumière excitatrice tombe sur le milieu d'amplification de manière efficace, grâce à la propriété géométrique de convergence d'une lumière, d'un foyer d'une ellipse sur l'autre foyer.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/d